nce=RFILE\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial message is a massive cobbler stitch task prompt with full project context, task description, execution constitution, go style constitution, and all supporting documentation. It requests implementation of cmd/chmod root protection (--preserve-root/--no-preserve-root) and reference mode (--reference=RFILE).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/chmod/main.go` to add:\n     1. `preserveRoot` and `reference` fields to the `options` struct\n     2. Parse `--preserve-root`, `--no-preserve-root`, and `--reference=RFILE` in argument parsing\n     3. Preserve-root logic in `processRecursive()` to refuse operating on `/` when `preserveRoot` is true (default when `-R` is used)\n     4. Reference file mode resolution in `main()` - read RFILE's mode and use it as the mode specification\n     5. Update `helpText` to document new flags\n   - Run `go build -o bin/chmod ./cmd/chmod/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/chmod/...` to verify no warnings (AC2)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/chmod/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two required files (srd089-chmod.yaml and cmd/chmod/main.go) and was about to begin implementing the changes. No code has been written yet. The implementation plan is:\n   \n   - Add `preserveRoot bool` and `reference string` to the `options` struct\n   - In `parseArgs()`, handle `--preserve-root`, `--no-preserve-root`, and `--reference=RFILE` (including `--reference RFILE` form)\n   - In `parseLongFlag()`, add cases for the new long flags\n   - Default `preserveRoot` to true when `-R` is set (matching GNU behavior)\n   - In `processRecursive()`, check at the start if `preserveRoot` is true and the resolved path is `/`, then print error and return\n   - In `main()`, if `opts.reference != \"\"`, read the reference file's mode and convert it to an octal mode string to pass to existing `processFile()` logic\n   - Update `helpText` constant\n\n9